<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · song</p><h1 class="enc-title">Brazilian National Anthem</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">music first played 13 April <a href="/years/1831">1831</a>; official words <a href="/years/1922">1922</a> (written <a href="/years/1909">1909</a>)</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Hino Nacional Brasileiro</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The music of the Brazilian National Anthem was composed by Francisco Manuel da Silva and first played in public on 13 April 1831. Days earlier, on 7 April, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a>'s first emperor, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pedro-i-of-brazil">Pedro I</a>, had abdicated, leaving his five-year-old son as Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pedro-ii-of-brazil">Pedro II</a>, and on 13 April the ship carrying him left the port of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rio-de-janeiro">Rio de Janeiro</a>.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The music of the <b>Brazilian National Anthem</b> was composed by Francisco Manuel da Silva and first played in public on 13 April 1831.</blockquote><a href="/songs/brazilian-national-anthem">Brazilian National Anthem</a></li></ul></section>
